  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They held the lead through six innings and handed it away in one.",
    "what_this_means": "Michael King gave them six innings of two-run ball. The lineup scratched out three runs against Clayton Kershaw, enough to be in front into the seventh. Then Adrian Morejon entered with two outs and nobody on, and the Dodgers scored four before anyone recorded the third out. That was the game. Jackson Merrill hit one for show. A solo shot in the fourth that briefly felt like it might matter. But the offense never produced when runners were already in scoring position. Eight runners left on base, one converted. This is what inconsistency looks like when the pitching refuses to break: the staff gives you a chance, and you don't take it.",
